---
description: "How to write and run StudyHub tests: pytest, Vitest, Playwright"
alwaysApply: false
---

- Backend: pytest, one test file per module in apps/api/tests; database fixtures – SQLite in-memory
  (see tests/conftest.py).
- Frontend: Vitest for hooks and pure functions; Playwright only for end-to-end scenarios.
- First a failing test, then the code. Do not weaken or delete existing assertions
  to make a test pass.
- For time, use a fixed clock in the test, not the current time.
- Before finishing, run the tests of the changed modules and report the result.
